# Testing Conventions

## ViewModel tests
```kotlin
class {Feature}ViewModelTest {
    private val fakeRepository = Fake{Feature}Repository()
    private val useCase = Get{Feature}UseCase(fakeRepository)
    private val viewModel = {Feature}ViewModel(TestDispatcherProvider(), useCase)

    @Test
    fun `load data updates state with success`() = runTest {
        fakeRepository.setResponse(Result.Success(testData))
        viewModel.sendIntent(Intent.Load{Feature})
        advanceUntilIdle()
        assertEquals(false, viewModel.state.value.isLoading)
        assertEquals(testData, viewModel.state.value.data)
    }
}
```

## Rules
- Tests in `src/commonTest/kotlin/` mirroring main source layout
- Use `TestDispatcherProvider` from `ijs-dispatcher-lib` for coroutine tests
- Use `runTest` from `kotlinx-coroutines-test`
- Fake implementations for repositories and data sources
- Test all three `Result` branches: Loading, Success, Error
- Test intent routing in `handleIntent`
- Naming: backtick-quoted descriptive names
